; ============================================================================
; AIF-087 M4 -- RECOVERY NON-REFIRE, STEP 3: OPEN AND LET RECOVERY RUN
;
; Status: CANDIDATE / explicit-run, driven from C++ by
;         run_trigger_recovery_nonrefire (REGRESSION TRIGGERVETO RECOVERY).
; Safety: MUTATING (SANDBOX only; the arm erases the fixture when it finishes)
;
; The C++ arm has just restored a REAL committed journal -- captured from this
; engine at the one instant it exists, between journal_begin_commit's COMMIT
; marker and journal_note_commit's delete -- next to the DBF. cmd_use.cpp:990
; calls recover_table_buffer_journal on open, which replays it.
;
; TRG_R1 IS THE DISCRIMINATOR FOR REPLAY, AND IT IS ALSO THE CONTROL FOR THE
; CLAIM THE ARM ACTUALLY MAKES. The arm asserts that the AFTER phase fired ZERO
; times across this window. Zero is also what you observe when nothing happened
; at all -- when the journal was not restored, or the table did not open, or
; recovery discarded the log. So the C++ side may not credit its zero unless
; this marker says the replay DID run. Never credit G1 without D1.
;
; Deliberately does NOT close: the liveness step needs this open area to prove
; the probe that read zero was alive the whole time.
; ============================================================================

SET ECHO OFF
STOP_ON_ERROR OFF
SET PATH DBF DBF/SANDBOX
SET PATH INDEXES INDEXES/SANDBOX
SET PATH LMDB LMDB/SANDBOX

FORMULA "TRGRECOV-REOPEN-BEGIN"

SELECT 1
CLOSE
USE TRGVETO
GO 1
? "TRG_R1_replay_restored_committed_value:" + (ALLTRIM(NAME) = "VETOED")

FORMULA "TRGRECOV-REOPEN-END"
